If you are on Windows, use these instructions to compile with MingW and 
patch with Cygwin.

21:42 1/3/2004Here's a quick start for building NetHack with MinGW:

( [] contains commands you type in at the command prompt)
   {gnudir} represents the location where you choose to install
            the gnuwin32 utilities below.)

  1. Obtain and install latest mingw from:
     http://prdownloads.sf.net/mingw/MinGW-3.1.0-1.exe?download
  2. Download the NetHack sources from Nethack.org
  3. Unpack the NetHack sources.
     Don't have a way to do that? Download and execute:
     http://prdownloads.sf.net/gnuwin32/gzip-1.3.5-bin.exe?download
     [{gnudir}\bin\gunzip nethack-343-src.tgz]
     Also download and execute:
     http://prdownloads.sf.net/gnuwin32/tar-1.13-1-bin.exe?download
     [{gnudir}\bin\tar -xvf nethack-342.tar]
  4. Go to the top of the NetHack source tree you just unpacked.
  5. [cd sys\winnt]
  6. [nhsetup.bat]
  7. [cd ..\..\src]
  8. Decide whether you want to build the tty version (NetHack.exe)
     or the gui version (NetHackW.exe). For the former (tty version),
     do nothing in this step, that is what the Makefile builds out
     of the box.
     For the gui version, use a text editor to edit Makefile.gcc and
     change the line:
             #GRAPHICAL = Y
     to
             GRAPHICAL = Y
     In other words, "uncomment that line."
  9. [mingw32-make -f Makefile.gcc install]
     ...much activity...
10. [cd ..\binary]
11. [nethack]
12. "Do you want your possessions identified?"

Additional note from Karl Garrison [paraphrased slightly]:
     If you also have cygwin installed on your system, you may have
     to set PATH so that only MinGW is in it; (e.g. path=c:\mingw\bin).
     Failure to do so prior to step 9 may lead to a munch of Makefile
     syntax errors, even if MinGW is in your PATH before cygwin, and
     you are using the correct make.

To patch:
patch -lp1 -F4 < (patch name).diff

To test patches use --dry-run

Hope this helps!
